# --- licensed datasets (MOBIUS/SBVPI, Univ. Ljubljana): non-commercial research licence,
# GDPR Art. 9 biometric data. They live OUTSIDE the repo (../datasets/); this is a backstop
# against an accidental copy-in + add. NEVER commit these. ---
datasets/

# --- data & generated outputs (privacy: real faces/eyes; also large) ---
data/
debug_frames/
debug_masks/
# ROI boxes / light-onset marks tied to the private clips; useless without them
eye_rois.json
new_subject_rois.json
light_onset.json

# --- images and video: ignored EVERYWHERE by extension (privacy: real faces/eyes; also large) ---
# Bracket patterns match any letter case, so IMG_1234.MOV or frame.PNG is caught even on a
# case-sensitive filesystem (macOS ignores case by default, Linux does not).
*.[pP][nN][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
*.[hH][eE][iI][cC]
*.[hH][eE][iI][fF]
*.[wW][eE][bB][pP]
*.[gG][iI][fF]
*.[bB][mM][pP]
*.[tT][iI][fF]
*.[tT][iI][fF][fF]
*.[mM][oO][vV]
*.[mM][pP]4
*.[mM]4[vV]
*.[aA][vV][iI]
*.[mM][kK][vV]
# Exception: the iOS app's asset catalogs (app icon, UI images) must be tracked or a fresh
# clone will not build. Never put eye footage in an asset catalog.
!apps/ios/**/*.xcassets/**

# Eye crops and full-face frames in labeling/ are covered by the image rules above. The
# hand-drawn label JSONs sitting beside them ARE tracked: coordinates only, no embedded
# imageData, and they are the source labelme_to_gt.py rebuilds labeling/gt.csv from.
labeling/frames/
labeling/label_session/
labeling/gt/
labeling/roi_previews/
# fine-tune model checkpoints (derived artifacts, large)
checkpoints/

# --- third-party: clone RITnet separately (see README), do not vendor its repo ---
RITnet/

# --- local working docs (not for the public repo) ---
CLAUDE.md
pupillometry_plan.md
optimizations_brainstorm.md
mobius-sbvpi-handoff.md

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- os / editor ---
.DS_Store
.vscode/

# local math notes (not for the repo)
circle_fit_math.md
